{"sounds":{"intro":"Gothic is the oldest Germanic language we have a real text in. It comes from the Bible that Bishop Wulfila (Ulfilas) translated in the 4th century AD. It died out centuries ago. The Latin spelling here is the scholars' transliteration of the Gothic alphabet. The sounds are reconstructed, and the Gothic alphabet itself is not shown because many devices cannot display it.","rows":[["þ","like \"th\" in \"thing\"","þu"],["ƕ","\"hw\", like the old Scots \"wh\" in \"which\"","ƕas"],["ai / aí","short \"e\", like \"bed\"; aí is the same sound in a few words","ains"],["ei","long \"ee\"","weis"],["au / aú","short \"o\", like \"more\" but short","augo"],["ô / ê / û","long \"oh\", long \"ay\", long \"oo\"","fôtus"],["g (before g, k)","\"ng\", as in \"sing\"","briggan"]],"notes":["Gothic nouns have three genders and four main cases. Many masculine nouns end in -s in the nominative: dags (day), wulfs (wolf), hlaifs (bread).","This pool is much smaller than the Spanish one on purpose. Gothic survives in only one main text (the Bible), so there are no words for modern things and some everyday words are missing. The pronunciation is reconstructed, and nothing has been checked by a specialist. Treat it as a first guide."]},"numbers":[{"id":"1-to-10","title":"1 to 10","items":[["one","ains","ens"],["two","twai","twe"],["three","þreis","threes"],["four","fidwôr","FID-wohr"],["five","fimf","fimf"],["six","saihs","ses"],["seven","sibun","SIB-oon"],["eight","ahtau","AKH-taw"],["nine","niun","NEE-oon"],["ten","taihun","TEH-hoon"]]},{"id":"bigger-numbers","title":"Bigger numbers","items":[["one hundred","hund","hoond"],["one thousand","þûsundi","THOO-soon-dee"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"greetings","title":"Greetings","items":[["hail","hails","hayls"],["well / good","waila","WEH-lah"],["yes","ja","yah"],["no","ne","neh"],["thanks","awiliud","AH-wee-lee-ood"],["peace","gawairþi","gah-WEHR-thee"],["I ask / please","bidja","BID-yah"]]}],"phrases":[{"id":"about-me","title":"About me","items":[["I","ik","ik"],["you (one)","þu","thoo"],["he","is","is"],["she","si","see"],["we","weis","wees"],["you (many)","jus","yoos"],["I am","ik im","ik im"],["you are","þu is","thoo is"],["he is","is ist","is ist"],["I know","ik wait","ik wet"],["I do not know","ik ni wait","ik nee wet"],["I see","ik saiƕa","ik SEH-hwah"],["what?","ƕa","hwah"],["who?","ƕas","hwahs"],["where?","ƕar","hwahr"]]}],"vocab":[{"id":"people-and-family","title":"People and family","items":[["father","atta","AT-tah"],["mother","aiþei","EH-thee"],["son","sunus","SOO-noos"],["daughter","dauhtar","DOW-tar"],["brother","broþar","BROH-thar"],["sister","swistar","SWIS-tar"],["man","manna","MAN-nah"],["woman","qinô","KWEE-noh"],["child","barn","barn"],["king","þiudans","THEE-oo-dans"],["lord","frauja","FROW-yah"],["god","guþ","gooth"]]},{"id":"nature-and-things","title":"Nature and things","items":[["sun","sunnô","SOON-noh"],["moon","mêna","MAY-nah"],["star","stairnô","STEHR-noh"],["sky","himins","HIM-ins"],["earth","airþa","EHR-thah"],["water","watô","WAH-toh"],["fire","fôn","fohn"],["city","baurgs","bowrgs"],["mountain","fairguni","FEHR-goo-nee"],["tree","triu","tree-oo"],["bread","hlaifs","hlefs"],["wine","wein","ween"],["fish","fisks","fisks"],["dog","hunds","hoonds"],["wolf","wulfs","woolfs"],["house","razn","rahzn"],["day","dags","dahgs"],["night","nahts","nahts"],["name","namô","NAH-moh"],["word","waurd","wowrd"]]},{"id":"body","title":"Body","items":[["hand","handus","HAN-doos"],["foot","fôtus","FOH-toos"],["eye","augô","OW-goh"],["ear","ausô","OW-soh"],["heart","hairtô","HEHR-toh"],["head","haubiþ","HOW-bith"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["good","goþs","gohths"],["bad / evil","ubils","OO-bils"],["big / great","mikils","MIK-ils"],["small","leitils","LEE-tils"],["new","niujis","NEE-oo-yis"],["old","alþeis","AL-thees"],["white","hweits","hwites"],["black","swarts","swahrts"]]},{"id":"verbs-to-do","title":"Verbs (to do)","items":[["to be","wisan","WEE-sahn"],["to eat","itan","EE-tahn"],["to drink","drigkan","DRING-kahn"],["to go","gaggan","GAHNG-gahn"],["to come","qiman","KWEE-mahn"],["to see","saiƕan","SEH-hwahn"],["to say","qiþan","KWEE-thahn"],["to give","giban","GEE-bahn"],["to love","frijôn","FREE-yohn"],["to live","liban","LEE-bahn"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Gothic has singular, dual (two) and plural for \"I\" and \"you\": wit (we two), jut (you two), weis (we, many), jus (you, many)."],"rows":[["I","ik","ik"],["you (one)","þu","thoo"],["he","is","is"],["she","si","see"],["it","ita","EE-tah"],["we two","wit","wit"],["we (many)","weis","wees"],["you (many)","jus","yoos"]],"ex":[["I am a king","ik im þiudans","ik im THEE-oo-dans"],["you are a man","þu is manna","thoo is MAN-nah"],["we are brothers","weis sijum broþrjus","wees SEE-yoom BROHTH-ryoos"]]},{"id":"to-be-wisan","title":"To be: wisan","text":["The verb \"to be\" changes for each person."],"rows":[["I am","im","im"],["you are","is","is"],["he / she / it is","ist","ist"],["we are","sijum","SEE-yoom"],["you (many) are","sijuþ","SEE-yooth"],["they are","sind","sind"]],"ex":[["I am good","ik im goþs","ik im gohths"],["he is a king","is ist þiudans","is ist THEE-oo-dans"],["they are men","sind mans","sind mahns"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"ni\" before the verb: \"ik ni wait\" (I do not know). For a ban, use \"ni\" with the verb: \"ni gagg\" (do not go)."],"rows":[["not","ni","nee"],["no one","ni manna","nee MAN-nah"]],"ex":[["I know","ik wait","ik wet"],["I do not know","ik ni wait","ik nee wet"],["he is good","is ist goþs","is ist gohths"],["he is not good","is ni ist goþs","is nee ist gohths"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["The command uses the verb stem: \"gagg\" (go!), \"qim\" (come!). Add \"ni\" to forbid."],"rows":[["go!","gagg!","gahng"],["come!","qim!","kweem"],["do not go","ni gagg","nee gahng"]],"ex":[["eat!","it!","it"],["do not eat!","ni it","nee it"]]}],"name":"Gothic","id":"got